citation-type="journal">Hannak, E., M. Kirkham, A.A. Hyman, and K. Oegema. <year>2001</year>. Aurora-A kinase is required for centrosome maturation in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic>. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>155</volume>:<fpage>1109</fpage>&#x02013;1116.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11748251</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Hannak, E., K. Oegema, M. Kirkham, P. G&#x000f6;nczy, B. Habermann, and A.A. Hyman. <year>2002</year>. The kinetically dominant assembly pathway for centrosomal asters in <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic> is &#x003b3;-tubulin dependent. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>157</volume>:<fpage>591</fpage>&#x02013;602.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12011109</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Heald, R., R. Tournebize, T. Blank, R. Sandaltzopoulos, P. Becker, A. Hyman, and E. Karsenti. <year>1996</year>. Self-organization of microtubules into bipolar spindles around artificial chromosomes in <italic>Xenopus</italic> egg extracts. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>382</volume>:<fpage>420</fpage>&#x02013;425.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8684481</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Hirota, T., N. Kunitoku, T. Sasayama, T. Marumoto, D. Zhang, M. Nitta, K. Hatakeyama, and H. Saya. <year>2003</year>. Aurora-A and an interacting activator, the LIM protein Ajuba, are required for mitotic commitment in human cells. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>585</fpage>&#x02013;598.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13678582</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Holmfeldt, P., S. Stenmark, and M. Gullberg. <year>2004</year>. Differential functional interplay of TOGp/XMAP215 and the KinI kinesin MCAK during interphase and mitosis. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>23</volume>:<fpage>627</fpage>&#x02013;637.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14749730</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Howard, J., and A.A. Hyman. <year>2003</year>. Dynamics and mechanics of the microtubule plus end. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>422</volume>:<fpage>753</fpage>&#x02013;758.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12700769</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Hyman, A., D. Drechsel, D. Kellogg, S. Salser, K. Sawin, P. Steffen, L. Wordeman, and T. Mitchison. <year>1991</year>. Preparation of modified tubulins. <source>Methods Enzymol.</source> <volume>196</volume>:<fpage>478</fpage>&#x02013;485.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2034137</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Job, D., O. Valiron, and B. Oakley. <year>2003</year>. Microtubule nucleation. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>111</fpage>&#x02013;117.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12517712</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Karsenti, E., and I. Vernos. <year>2001</year>. The mitotic spindle: a self-made machine. <source>Science.</source> <volume>294</volume>:<fpage>543</fpage>&#x02013;547.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11641489</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Khodjakov, A., and C.L. Rieder. <year>1999</year>. The sudden recruitment of &#x003b3;-tubulin to the centrosome at the onset of mitosis and its dynamic exchange throughout the cell cycle, do not require microtubules. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>146</volume>:<fpage>585</fpage>&#x02013;596.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10444067</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Kinoshita, K., I. Arnal, A. Desai, D.N. Drechsel, and A.A. Hyman. <year>2001</year>. Reconstitution of physiological microtubule dynamics using purified components. <source>Science.</source> <volume>294</volume>:<fpage>1340</fpage>&#x02013;1343.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11701928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Kinoshi